  speaker: 3
  text: 'The corridor ends at the gate and the gate does not open fast enough. The
    crews'' vans turn the corner. The sky does its morning work.


    The Shadow
    reaches her not as a hand but as a hush: names gone quiet, a night folded up
    like a finished exam.


    She wakes on the pavement with the box still shut,
    and the school - patient, gentle, terrible - keeps her mother''s memory the way
    a library keeps a book nobody borrowed.


    Dawn comes. It simply comes without
    her.'
  localizationKeys:
  - DAWNLESS
  - The night ran out. The school keeps what she could not carry.
